input_prompt: Explain what on-device AI means in simple terms.
INFO: Loaded OpenCL library with dlopen.


On-device AI is like having a smart computer that does its own thinking and learning, all while you're using it. Instead of sending data to a remote server (like a big server on the internet) to process it, the AI works on the device itself. This means it can make quick decisions, like adjusting your smart home devices based on your habits, without needing to connect to the internet. It also helps keep your data private, since it doesn't store or send it to others.

